\emph{Setting and inputs.} The fields and the unit are those of Definition \claimref{obj.field-theory.single-algebra-field}; the loop conventions are those of Proposition \claimref{synthesis.one-loop-qed-in-the-spacetime-algebra}: the Dirac matrices are the vectors of $\Cl(1,3)$, the units of the Feynman rules and of the Wick rotation are the field theory's unit $I_{4}$, numbers read in $\mathrm{span}\{1, I_{4}\}$ and collected outside each Clifford product as the right unit (clause (5) there: on a massive line the unit cannot act inside the product), and the trace is $\mathrm{Tr}\,X = 4\langle Xangle_{0}$ (clause (1), checked there and here against Dirac matrices over $\mathrm{span}_{\mathbb{Q}}\{1, I_{5}\}$, their complex scalar read as the central $I_{5} = I_{4}e$ of $\Cl(2,3)$, \claimref{std-algebra.complexification-is-the-odd-extension}). The chirality $\gamma_{5}$ acts as $x \mapsto I_{4}xI_{4}$, the right $I_{4}$ the unit, the coefficient; then $\gamma_{5}^{2}$ is $x \mapsto I_{4}^{2}xI_{4}^{2} = x$, $\gamma_{5}$ anticommutes with every vector, and in the Dirac representation, where it is the matrix of $I_{4}$ times the matrices' complex scalar, it is the usual off-diagonal identity (checked). Imported (Fact \claimref{synthesis.imported-one-loop-integrals-and-pauli-villars-regulators}): Feynman parametrisation, the Wick-rotated integral $\int rac{d^{4}\ell}{(2\pi)^{4}}(\ell^{2} - \Delta)^{-3} = -I_{4}/(32\pi^{2}\Delta)$, and Pauli-Villars regulator fields with weights of either sign. Every Clifford identity below is exact and is checked over the Gaussian rationals at rational momenta and masses.

\emph{(i) Trace.} Every blade but the scalar is traceless, so $\mathrm{Tr}(\gamma_{5}X) = 4\langle I_{4}Xangle_{0}\,I_{4}$, the unit in front. For four vectors only the grade-four part of $abcd$ contributes, $a\wedge b\wedge c\wedge d = \lambda I_{4}$, and $\langle I_{4}\lambda I_{4}angle_{0} = -\lambda$; so $\mathrm{Tr}(\gamma_{5}abcd) = -4\lambda I_{4}$, totally antisymmetric because the outer product is (checked on two orderings of four sample vectors and on the frame, $\langle I_{4}\gamma_{0}\gamma_{1}\gamma_{2}\gamma_{3}angle_{0} = -1$).

